linux-zako

Patch queue for Linux-libre with the Zen patchset and the BORE scheduler.
Patches only: no kernel tree, no build scripts, no releases.

Baseline: linux-libre 7.3.5 gnu tarball
Source: https://www.linux-libre.fsfla.org/pub/linux-libre/releases/7.3.5-gnu/
SHA-256: 00f30f9cc4328a4b0a8d8a71349f9dc9fabed762f0a27993160e319377ef5753

Apply in the order listed in series/7.3:

    tar xf linux-libre-7.3.5-gnu.tar.xz
    cd linux-libre-7.3.5
    git apply ../patches/7.3/0001-zen-7.3.5-zen1.patch
    git apply ../patches/7.3/0002-sched-bore-7.0.0.patch
    make olddefconfig
    make LOCALVERSION=-zako1

Leave CONFIG_SCHED_ALT (BMQ, PDS) off. It drops cgroup v2 cpu.weight and
cpu.max, sched_ext and SCHED_CORE.

Tags are named vX.Y.Z-zakoN and are never moved or deleted.

The queue moves to a new version only when Linux-libre, Zen and BORE have all
reached it.
